data.content:
Here are the three EF Core 10 breaking changes affecting your code and how to fix each:

---

## 1. `ExecuteUpdateAsync` — now accepts a regular lambda (not an expression tree)

Your complex expression tree construction **won't compile**. Replace it with a simple lambda:

```csharp
// .NET 10 — dramatically simplified
await context.Blogs.ExecuteUpdateAsync(s =>
{
    s.SetProperty(b => b.Views, 8);
    if (nameChanged)
    {
        s.SetProperty(b => b.Name, "foo");
    }
});
```

No more `Expression.Lambda`, `Expression.Call`, or manual tree stitching needed.

---

## 2. Complex type column names — uniquified and full-path nested

Two changes apply:

- **Duplicate property names** (e.g., `ShippingAddress.Street` and `BillingAddress.Street`) now get a numeric suffix appended automatically.
- **Nested complex types** use the full path: `Order.Payment.BillingAddress.City` maps to `Payment_BillingAddress_City` (was `BillingAddress_City`).

Both generate rename migrations. **Fix:** pin existing column names explicitly:

```csharp
modelBuilder.Entity<Customer>(b =>
{
    b.ComplexProperty(c => c.ShippingAddress, a =>
    {
        a.Property(x => x.Street).HasColumnName("ShippingAddress_Street");
    });
    b.ComplexProperty(c => c.BillingAddress, a =>
    {
        a.Property(x => x.Street).HasColumnName("BillingAddress_Street");
    });
});

// For nested:
modelBuilder.Entity<Order>(b =>
{
    b.ComplexProperty(o => o.Payment, p =>
    {
        p.ComplexProperty(pay => pay.BillingAddress, ba =>
        {
            ba.Property(x => x.City).HasColumnName("BillingAddress_City");
        });
    });
});
```

---

## 3. `IRelationalCommandDiagnosticsLogger` — new `logCommandText` parameter

All methods gained a `string logCommandText` parameter (redacted SQL for safe logging). Add it:

```csharp
public class MyLogger : IRelationalCommandDiagnosticsLogger
{
    public InterceptionResult<DbDataReader> CommandReaderExecuting(
        IRelationalConnection connection,
        DbCommand command,
        DbContext context,
        Guid commandId,
        Guid connectionId,
        DateTimeOffset startTime,
        string logCommandText)  // ← new parameter
    {
        // Use logCommandText for logging (constants may be redacted)
        // Use command.CommandText for actual SQL
    }
}
```

Update all method signatures in your implementation (`CommandReaderExecuted`, `CommandScalarExecuting`, etc.) similarly.
